WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/notifications/components/NotificationGroupRow.tsx — renders ONE server-aggregated
  notification thread. Composes the latest member as a `NotificationRow`; the grouping affordances live OUTSIDE
  that row:
      isSingleton = group.group_key == null
      extraCount  = max(0, group.count - 1)
      chrome shows when  !isSingleton && (extraCount > 0 || unread_count > 1):
        • "+N similar" expand/collapse caret (ChevronRight/Down) → lazily fetches members on expand
          (useGroupMembers, gated `enabled: expanded && !isSingleton`)
        • unread-count chip · "{{count}} vehicles affected" hint
        • "Mark group read" ghost Button → useBulkMarkRead({group_key}) → useToast success/error
      expanded member region (role="region") omits the latest (members.filter(m => m.id !== latest.id)) and
      renders membersLoading / membersError / "No thread members found" / the member rows.
  Singletons (group_key === null) render as a plain row with the grouping chrome hidden.
  Data sources (bound via the P1/S8 seam, no view HTTP): useNotifications, useGroupMembers, useBulkMarkRead,
  useToast, useTranslation, useId.

